lor on the diagonal values, etc.) the three confusion matrices (on the test set), which do you think is the best method? Why? (0.50 point)                                                      \n#### I think the Neural Networrk is the best method. It achieves the highest number of correctly classified samples (strong diagonal) and the fewest misclassifications.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"####  Based on the mean validation accuracies (from the 5-fold cross-validation) for the three methods. Which is the best method? (0.25 point)\n#### The Neural Network (MLPClassifier) is the best method based on the mean validation accuracies from the 5-fold cross-validation.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"####  Compute the accuracies for the three methods on the test set. Which is the best method? (0.25 point)\n####  Compute the F-measure for the three methods on the test set. Which is the best method? (0.25 point)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"test_results=[]\nfor name,model in trained_models.items():\n    y_pred=model.predict(X_test_std)\n    acc=accuracy_score(y_test,y_pred)\n    prec=precision_score(y_test, y_pred,average='macro',zero_division=0)\n    rec=recall_score(y_test,y_pred,average='macro',zero_division=0)\n    f1=f1_score(y_test,y_pred,average='macro',zero_division=0)\n    test_results.append({\n        'Classifier': name,\n        'Accuracy (Test)': acc,\n        'Precision (Test)': prec,\n        'Recall (Test)': rec,\n        'F1-score (Test)': f1\n    })\ntest_df=pd.DataFrame(test_results)\nprint(\"\\nTest Set Performance Results:\\n\")\nprint(test_df.round(4))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-31T04:48:04.587128Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-31T04:48:04.587403Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-31T04:48:04.661014Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-10-31T04:48:04.587383Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-31T04:48:04.659994Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\nTest Set Performance Results:\n\n                       Classifier  Accuracy (Test)  Precision (Test)  \\\n0        Naive Bayes (GaussianNB)           0.5036            0.5498   \n1  Neural Network (MLPClassifier)           0.8215            0.8134   \n2             Adaboost Classifier           0.6430            0.6361   \n\n   Recall (Test)  F1-score (Test)  \n0         0.5112           0.4732  \n1         0.8131           0.8121  \n2         0.6353           0.6339  \n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":11},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### The Neural Network is the best method based on test set accuracy. It shows the strongest ability to correctly classify unseen MRI images.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### The Neural Network is the best method based on the F-measure. It achieves the most balanced performance between recall and precision.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"###  7. (Model Selection) Use images from TWO classes. Perform a standard 5-fold cross-validation and a stratified 5-fold cross-validation on the training set (i.e., the standardized edge histogram dataset obtained from the training set) for Support Vector Classifiers using LinearSVC such that parameter 𝐶 =0.1,1,10,100 and other parameters set as default. (2.5 points)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"selected_classes=['glioma','meningioma']\nmask=np.isin(y_train, selected_classes)\nX_two=X_train_std[mask]\ny_two=y_train[mask]\nprint(f\"Subset shape:X_two={X_two.shape},y_two={y_two.shape}\")\nC_values=[0.1,1,10,100]\nresults_standard,results_stratified=[],[]\ntrain_errors_standard,val_errors_standard=[],[]\ntrain_errors_stratified,val_errors_stratified=[],[]\nfor C in C_values:\n    svc=LinearSVC(C=C,random_state=42,max_iter=20000,tol=1e-3,dual=False)\n    kf=KFold(n_splits=5,shuffle=True,random_state=42)\n    scores_kf=cross_val_score(svc,X_two,y_two,cv=kf,scoring='accuracy')\n    results_standard.append({\n        'C': C,'CV Type':'Stan